      "question": "Curve C1 has equation xy = 15/2 - 5x, x not 0. Curve C2 has equation y = x^3 - 7/2 x - 5. Show that C1 and C2 meet when 2x^4 - 7x^2 - 15 = 0.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "Show: substitute y from C2 into C1 and multiply through by 2 to get 2x^4 - 7x^2 - 15 = 0.",
      "steps": [
        "Substitute y = x^3 - 7/2 x - 5 into xy = 15/2 - 5x.",
        "Left side: x(x^3 - 7/2 x - 5) = x^4 - 7/2 x^2 - 5x.",
        "The -5x on both sides cancels: x^4 - 7/2 x^2 = 15/2.",
        "Multiply by 2: 2x^4 - 7x^2 = 15.",
        "Rearrange: 2x^4 - 7x^2 - 15 = 0, as required."
      ],
