      "question": "Curves C1 (xy = 15/2 - 5x, x not 0) and C2 (y = x^3 - 7/2 x - 5) meet at points P and Q. Using algebra, find the exact distance PQ.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "PQ = sqrt(65)",
      "steps": [
        "Factorise 2x^4 - 7x^2 - 15 = (2x^2 + 3)(x^2 - 5).",
        "2x^2 + 3 = 0 has no real roots, so x^2 = 5 and x = +/- sqrt(5).",
        "For x = sqrt5: y = 5sqrt5 - 3.5sqrt5 - 5 = 3sqrt5/2 - 5, so P = (sqrt5, 3sqrt5/2 - 5).",
        "For x = -sqrt5: y = -3sqrt5/2 - 5, so Q = (-sqrt5, -3sqrt5/2 - 5).",
        "Differences: dx = 2sqrt5 and dy = 3sqrt5.",
        "PQ = sqrt((2sqrt5)^2 + (3sqrt5)^2) = sqrt(20 + 45) = sqrt(65), about 8.06."
      ],
