      "question": "Solve the simultaneous equations y + 4x + 1 = 0 and y^2 + 5x^2 + 2x = 0.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "(x, y) = (-1/7, -3/7) and (-1/3, 1/3)",
      "steps": [
        "From the linear equation: y = -4x - 1.",
        "Substitute: (4x + 1)^2 + 5x^2 + 2x = 0.",
        "Expand: 16x^2 + 8x + 1 + 5x^2 + 2x = 0, so 21x^2 + 10x + 1 = 0.",
        "Factorise or use the formula: (7x + 1)(3x + 1) = 0, so x = -1/7 or x = -1/3.",
        "x = -1/7 gives y = 4/7 - 1 = -3/7.",
        "x = -1/3 gives y = 4/3 - 1 = 1/3."
      ],
